{
  "about": "layout is the parser path a file takes (alignment.parse_matrix_csv): dia-nn is its Genes-column path, matrix its plain first-column path. The diagnostic bank (research/value-scale-plan.md, Step 1): real tables whose scale is known from provenance, fixed on 2026-10-28 before any statistic was computed on them. Every later step is checked against them. Bank accessions count as looked at, so the calibration and test corpora exclude them. label_strength: documented = the software's or authors' documentation says it; named = a column, layer or file name says it; author_code = the authors' own analysis code treats it so; inferred = reasoned from the values (kept as a known case, never used to calibrate).",
  "quotes": {
    "diann": {"quote": "These contain normalised QuantUMS or MaxLFQ quantities for protein groups ('pg_matrix'), gene groups ('gg_matrix'), as well as normalised quantities for precursors ('pr_matrix'). ... If the data needs to be log-transformed, these zeroes can be replaced with NA values.", "source": "https://github.com/vdemichev/DiaNN (README, read 2026-10-28)"},
    "maxquant": {"quote": "Summed up eXtracted Ion Current (XIC) of all isotopic clusters associated with the identified AA sequence.", "source": "https://cox-labs.github.io/coxdocs/output_tables.html (the Intensity columns; LFQ intensity is their normalised form; read 2026-10-28)"},
    "fragpipe": {"quote": "normalized (by default) protein intensity using the razor peptides (from the MaxLFQ method)", "source": "https://fragpipe.nesvilab.org/docs/tutorial_fragpipe_outputs.html ([experiment] MaxLFQ Intensity; read 2026-10-28)"},
    "spectronaut": {"quote": "PG.AvgLog2Quantity", "source": "column of Spectronaut's own protein pivot report beside the per-run PG.Quantity columns (PXD049412, JB_250pgHeLa_50SPD_SO_MBR_Report_Protein_JB_Pivot_.tsv header, read 2026-10-28): the report logs PG.Quantity itself, so PG.Quantity is the quantity before the log"},
    "proteome_discoverer": {"quote": "They calculate a protein abundance as the simple summation of its associated and used peptide group abundances.", "source": "https://docs.thermofisher.com/r/Proteome-Discoverer-3.1-User-Guide/en-US1324937483v1 (read 2026-10-28)"},
    "ibaqpy": {"quote": "the iBAQ value is calculated as `Total precursor intensities / Number of observable peptides`", "source": "https://github.com/bigbio/ibaqpy (README, read 2026-10-28)"},
    "furtwangler_layers": {"quote": "layers: batchcorr, batchcorr_norm, batchcorr_norm_log2, batchcorr_norm_log2_imputed, batchcorr_norm_log2_nan, batchcorr_norm_log2fc_nan, log2_raw_sn", "source": "the h5ad's own layer names, each step named by the authors (read 2026-10-28); benchmark/datasets.py:273"}
  },
